  "area": "Source reference on other Evidence/dependent nodes",
  "why": "The new update matches any page whose title contains the Source's title, so Evidence naming the Source is found by a substring scan, and nodes that merely mention the title could be caught."
}
{
  "id": "s-evidence-already-linked-to-a-source",
  "area": "Evidence already linked to a Source",
  "why": "The update is filtered on reference_content->>sourceDocument being null, so it must not overwrite a reference that already exists."
}
{
  "id": "s-evidence-published-later-with-edits",
  "area": "Evidence published later with edits",
  "why": "The change deliberately avoids re-upserting the Evidence, so its stored title/body and edit time must stay as they were while only the reference changes."
}
{
  "id": "s-sources-with-unusual-or-imported",
  "area": "Sources with unusual or imported identity",
  "why": "Dependents are matched via sourceIdOfNode, which returns an RID for imported Sources while the restore keys by the local Source uid."
}
{
  "id": "s-publish-of-non-source-nodes-claims",
  "area": "Publish of non-Source nodes (Claims, Questions)",
  "why": "The title scan is meant to run only when a Source node is among those published, so ordinary publishes should be unaffected."
}
{
  "id": "s-source-node-type-naming-and-settings",
  "area": "Source node type naming and settings",
  "why": "The Source type is found by sourceSlotSchemaId, which looks for a node type named 'source' or falls back to the default id, and Evidence is found by a {source} placeholder in its format."
}
