CLAIM: Publishing a Source from Roam sets the source reference on Evidence that was published before it without one, and publishes nothing else. Evidence whose Source isn't in the space still warns and omits the reference.
GIVEN: A Roam graph signed in to the proof database with node sharing on and sync off, in the eng-2329-demo group. It holds a Source, two Evidence nodes naming it (A and B) and a third Evidence node (C) naming a second Source that stays unpublished. None of them is in the database yet.

=== evidence-first-no-reference [ticket]
T: Publishing Evidence before its Source stores it without a source reference
C: Evidence A has a concept in the space and its reference_content has no sourceDocument
Cap: Evidence A names a Source that isn't in the database yet. Publishing it stores the node, with no source reference.
P: the starting state of the Evidence-then-Source order: Evidence A is stored without its source reference
  - start from a quiet screen   {use=ui.quiet null}
  - share Evidence A, whose Source is not published yet   {use=share.current-node {"title":"[[EVD]] - PK 2329 evidence A - [[@PK 2329 source]]"}}
  - pick the eng-2329-demo group   {{"js":"proof.setSwitch('eng-2329-demo', true)"}}
  - publish it   {{"click":".bp3-dialog:visible .bp3-dialog-footer button:has-text(\"Publish\")"}}
  - wait for the publish result   {{"wait_for":".bp3-toast"}}
  - hold on the result   {{"pause":2}}

=== source-after-evidence-restores [ticket]
T: Publishing the Source afterwards sets the Evidence's source reference
C: Evidence A's reference_content.sourceDocument is the id of the Source's concept
Cap: Now the Source is published. Evidence A, which is not published again, gets its reference to the Source.
P: Done When 1: Publishing Evidence, then its Source, stores the Evidence's source reference, so importing that Evidence can import the Source and resolve its title without the missing-source warning.
  - start from a quiet screen   {use=ui.quiet null}
  - share the Source Evidence A names   {use=share.current-node {"title":"@PK 2329 source"}}
  - pick the eng-2329-demo group   {{"js":"proof.setSwitch('eng-2329-demo', true)"}}
  - publish it   {{"click":".bp3-dialog:visible .bp3-dialog-footer button:has-text(\"Publish\")"}}
  - wait for the publish result   {{"wait_for":".bp3-toast"}}
  - hold on the result   {{"pause":2}}

=== source-grants-no-other-node [ticket]
T: Publishing the Source publishes no other node
C: Evidence B and Evidence C have no concept, content or access row in the space; the only nodes published so far are the Source and Evidence A
Cap: Evidence B also names the Source, but it was never published. Publishing the Source left it alone.
P: Done When 2: Publishing a Source does not publish or grant access to any other node.


=== missing-source-warns [ticket]
T: Evidence whose Source is not in the space still warns and omits the reference
C: a toast says the Source is not in this space yet, and Evidence C is stored with no sourceDocument
Cap: Evidence C names a Source that was never published. Publishing it warns about the missing Source and stores no reference.
