[![Devin Review](https://uploads.linear.app/a22a96b9-57e1-4add-a306-7b596f0b7ee3/f9d50849-a4fe-45e2-a828-4a994a7e9d19/78b7575f-06ad-42e9-bf5a-8ea2a0682c5d)](<https://app.devin.ai/review/discoursegraphs/discourse-graph/pull/1493>)","createdAt":"2026-09-28T16:10:13.000Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-28T16:10:22.145Z","editedAt":null,"resolvedAt":null,"resolvedBy":null,"externalThreadId":null,"anchor":null,"author":{"id":"e261103a-8e4a-402c-bc4d-404274473428","name":"Devin","type":"externalUser"},"replies":[]},{"id":"7a087d56-588c-47eb-99c3-9240cc9e0e6a","body":"🟡 **Cached node types skip Source restoration**

When a dependent's UID has a stale cached type, `findDiscourseNode` ignores the title supplied by `restoreSourceReferences`. An Evidence cached as another type is skipped, leaving its published Source reference empty.

+++ Learn more

The [findDiscourseNode](<https://github.com/discoursegraphs/discourse-graph/blob/f8e16089eb4f8e062602339828734ec0a7e216a3/apps/roam/src/utils/findDiscourseNode.ts#L20-L38>) cache returns a stored result by UID before considering the supplied title or nodes. Ordinary page-title edits do not invalidate that cache. The new scan uses this cached result to choose whether and how to parse a candidate's Source, so a stale cached type or `false` skips a valid Evidence. This can persist across repeated Source publishes until the type cache is invalidated.

**Example:** A page was previously classified as a Claim, then renamed to an Evidence title that names `@A` and published before Source A. Publishing Source A scans the new Evidence title but receives the old Claim schema from the UID cache; the stored Evidence remains without its Source.

**Recommended fix:** Classify scan candidates from their title using a fresh match rather than the UID cache, or make `findDiscourseNode` re-evaluate cached entries when a supplied title differs. Account for the stored-title versus live-title distinction when choosing the authoritative classification.

+++

[![Devin Review](https://uploads.linear.app/a22a96b9-57e1-4add-a306-7b596f0b7ee3/f9d50849-a4fe-45e2-a828-4a994a7e9d19/78b7575f-06ad-42e9-bf5a-8ea2a0682c5d)](<https://app.devin.ai/review/discoursegraphs/discourse-graph/pull/1493>)

